---
description: Rules for the dashboard (single-file HTML/JS served by the app)
globs: scheduler/static/dashboard.html
alwaysApply: false
---

- One self-contained file: vanilla JS, no framework, no build step, **no CDN scripts** (the app must work offline/anywhere).
- Talk only to the app's own `/api/*` with the `api()` helper. It sends the `X-CSRF-Token` header from the
  `<meta name="csrf">` tag (the server replaces `__CSRF__`).
- Build DOM only with `h()` and `textContent`. **Never use `innerHTML`** with server or user data.
- Never put secret values in the page. The API only returns `secrets[name] = {set, from_env, hint}`.
- Choice lists (models, efforts, days, channels) come from `/api/state`. Don't hard-code them.
- Text must be plain, beginner-friendly English, and errors must say what to do next.
- Must work at phone width (no sideways scroll) and in dark mode (CSS variables in `:root`).
- After changes run `.venv/bin/python qa/e2e.py` and look at `qa/screenshots/`.
